  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[judged-by-a-cat]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[Get Judged by a Cat]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Upload your life choices. Receive a look.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Slow Blink
Silent Stare
Table Shove
Tail Verdict]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Acquire judgemental cats | We need 500 cats with opinions. So far we have one, and she is on a break.
Judgement as a Service | JaaS. An API where you POST your life choices and GET a look.
Scale contempt globally | Multi-region disdain with 99.9% uptime. The cats sleep 16 hours a day, so: SLA issues.
Enterprise: get judged at work | A cat reviews your pull requests. It approves nothing. It just sits on the keyboard.
Cat talent pipeline | Recruit, onboard and retain cats. The retention plan is a cardboard box.
Verdict analytics | A dashboard of how disappointed the cat is over time. The trend is flat. Flatly disappointed.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Outfit review | As a user, I want a cat to review my outfit so that I can change before any human sees it.
Slow blink of approval | As a user, I want one slow blink so that I feel something. Anything.
Judge from a height | As a cat, I want to judge from the top of the fridge so that the power dynamic is clear.
Ignore mode | As a cat, I want to ignore the request completely so that the user understands their place.
Second opinion | As a user, I want a second cat so that I can be judged by committee.
Judge the estimate | As a developer, I want the cat to look at my estimate so that somebody finally says it.
Paid in tuna | As a cat, I want my invoices paid in tuna so that I never have to talk to Finance.
A category for dogs | As a cat, I want a category for dogs so that I can leave it blank on purpose.
Appeal the verdict | As a user, I want to appeal so that the cat can ignore me twice.
A friendlier cat | As a client, I want a friendlier cat so that conversion goes up. The cat has read the request.
Timesheets for cats | As a PM, I want cats to log hours so that I can explain 14 hours of 'stared out of window'.
3 AM availability | As a cat, I want to deliver verdicts at 03:00 so that the user is awake to receive them.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Silent Stare | The core product. Eight seconds of eye contact. No refunds.
Table Shove | The cat slowly pushes your submission off a table. Premium only.
Tail Verdict | Up: acceptable. Twitching: reconsider. Puffed: delete your account.
Verdict PDF | A formal certificate. It is a paw print and the word 'hm'.
Lap mode | The cat sits on you. This is not approval. It is a heating decision.
Box integration | If it fits, it sits. If it sits, your ticket is blocked.
Laser pointer login | Two-factor: follow the red dot. Cats pass. Users do not.
Purr-o-meter | Measures purring on a scale from 0 to 'that is actually the fridge'.
Keyboard takeover | The cat walks across your message before it sends. Usually an improvement.
Sunbeam scheduling | The cat is only available where the sun hits the floor. Bookings move with it.
Availability status | The cat is 'Away'. The cat has been 'Away' since March.
Breakfast reminder | Alerts you at 05:00 that the bowl is half empty, which means empty.
Hairball report | A monthly summary of everything the cat could not stomach. Includes your CV.
Favourite human | The cat picks one person. It is the one who is allergic.
Door mode | Cat wants in. Cat wants out. The feature toggles itself.
Gift delivery | Top users get a 'present' on the doormat. Cannot be disabled.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Cat approved something | Critical. The cat showed warmth in production. Roll back immediately.
Verdict returns 'meow' | Expected: a judgement. Actual: 'meow'. Product says that is the judgement.
Cat asleep on the server | It is warm there. We cannot move her. Uptime now depends on a nap.
Dog in the cat pool | It rates everything 'AMAZING!!'. Users love it. The brand is at risk.
Stare never ends | Session timeout is not respected. One user has been looked at since Tuesday.
Cucumber crashes everything | Repro: place cucumber behind cat. The whole platform jumps one metre.
Cat pushed prod off the table | It looked at us while doing it. No rollback. Root cause: cat.
Verdict sent to wrong human | My boss got judged for my haircut. He agrees with the cat.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[Single point of failure | There is one cat. Her name is Misty. No backup, no handover document.
Scratching post architecture | Nine teams have clawed at this codebase. Nobody remembers its original shape.
Legacy litter box | Nobody cleaned up after the last vendor. We just add more sand on top.
if (cat.isHungry) everywhere | 412 places check whether the cat is hungry. The answer is always true.
Zoomies-driven development | Half the commits were made at 02:00 at full speed. No comments, only claw marks.
Untested on other cats | Works with Misty. The neighbour's cat 'has a different API'.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[CEO Request: A more positive cat | 'More of a can-do attitude.' The cat was in the room. The cat did not blink.
CEO Request: Judge our competitors | 'Publicly. On LinkedIn.' Legal has left the chat.
CEO Request: Cat at the all-hands | 'Ten minutes, a few slides.' The cat declined the invite without a note.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[You have been seen. It is not impressed.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[Upload your outfit, your life choices or your pull request. A real cat looks at it for two seconds, then at the wall. That is the feedback.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Request judgement]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Brutally silent feedback | No words, no stars, no NPS. Just a slow blink and the feeling that you should have known better.
Enterprise-grade disdain | SLA: your work is ignored within four business hours. Premium customers get it pushed off a table.
Human in the loop | A human is involved. They open the tin. That is the full extent of their decision-making power.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[It looked at my CV, then sat on it. I got the job. I don't know what this means.
We replaced code review with the cat. Same turnaround, clearer signals.
I got a slow blink. My therapist says that's a nine out of ten.
It knocked my coffee off the desk mid-demo. Most honest feedback I had all year.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[One tin of tuna per judgement. No refunds. The cat does not do refunds. The cat does not do anything.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© Get Judged by a Cat. All judgements are final. Complaints may be placed in the litter tray.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
